IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-dates`

-- Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) -- the law the seat module uses: the s 4 meaning of improper conduct, the
-- s 9 test of a public interest disclosure with its exclusions (ss 9(3), 19, 20), the entities a disclosure may or must go
-- to (ss 13 to 17) and the people who may receive it for them (s 12, Schedule 2), the s 3 and s 43 meaning of detrimental
-- action in reprisal, the receiving entity's duty to advise the discloser within 28 days (s 24) as a regulative rule with
-- its trace helper, the s 54 circumstances in which a confidential disclosure may be passed on, and the table of offences
-- and penalties. The questions are in pid-seat.l4.
--
-- The Act's terms are kept, each with a plain gloss. Judgments the Act leaves to someone else ("reasonably believes",
-- "considers", "honestly believed", "trivial", "substantial", "reasonable precautions") are inputs, never decided here.
-- Terms borrowed from other Acts ("corrupt conduct" from the IBAC Act 2011, "public service body" and "public entity" from
-- the Public Administration Act 2004, "Councillor" from the Local Government Act 2020) are asked as facts.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Public Interest
-- Disclosures Act 2012, Version No. 032 (2 October 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 -- shared rules`

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`as an answer` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 4 -- improper conduct`

-- s 4(1)(b): "conduct of a public officer or public body engaged in by the public officer or public body in their
-- capacity as a public officer or a public body that constitutes" one of eight things.
DECLARE `Public officer conduct` IS ONE OF
    `a criminal offence`
    `serious professional misconduct`
    `dishonest performance of public functions`
    `an intentional or reckless breach of public trust`
    `an intentional or reckless misuse of information or material acquired in performing public functions`
    `a substantial mismanagement of public resources`
    `a substantial risk to the health or safety of one or more persons`
    `a substantial risk to the environment`
    `none of the s 4(1)(b) kinds`

DECLARE `Conduct facts` HAS
    `the conduct is corrupt conduct`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the kind of public officer conduct`                          IS A `Public officer conduct`
    `the conduct was in the capacity of a public officer or body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct adversely affects honest public performance`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is meant to adversely affect effective public performance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct got someone a gain they would not otherwise have obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct could be a conspiracy or attempt to do any of that` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is trivial`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is for the Court of Disputed Returns`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(1) "improper conduct means" (a) to (d): a "means" definition, so no head is JUST FALSE. s 4(2) "conduct that is
-- trivial does not constitute improper conduct" and s 4(3) "This Act does not apply to any conduct ... that can be
-- considered by the Court of Disputed Returns": flat negatives, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN f IS A `Conduct facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- improper conduct` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF f's `the conduct is for the Court of Disputed Returns` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF f's `the conduct is trivial` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE `as an answer` (`s 4(1)(a)` OR `s 4(1)(b)` OR `s 4(1)(c)(i)` OR `s 4(1)(c)(ii)` OR `s 4(1)(d)`)
    WHERE
        `s 4(1)(a)` MEANS f's `the conduct is corrupt conduct`
        `s 4(1)(b)` MEANS
                (NOT (f's `the kind of public officer conduct` EQUALS `none of the s 4(1)(b) kinds`))
            AND f's `the conduct was in the capacity of a public officer or body`
        `s 4(1)(c)(i)` MEANS f's `the conduct adversely affects honest public performance`
        `s 4(1)(c)(ii)` MEANS
                f's `the conduct is meant to adversely affect effective public performance`
            AND f's `the conduct got someone a gain they would not otherwise have obtained`
        `s 4(1)(d)` MEANS f's `the conduct could be a conspiracy or attempt to do any of that`

§§ `s 9 -- what the information shows`

-- s 9(1)(a) "information that shows or tends to show", (b) "information that the person reasonably believes shows or
-- tends to show". Whether it does is a judgment, asked.
DECLARE `How the information bears on it` IS ONE OF
    `the information shows or tends to show it`
    `I reasonably believe the information shows or tends to show it`
    `neither`

-- s 9(1)(a)(i), (ii): improper conduct by "a person, public officer or public body", or detrimental action "against a
-- person in contravention of section 45" by "a public officer or public body".
DECLARE `What the information is about` IS ONE OF
    `improper conduct by a person, public officer or public body`
    `detrimental action by a public officer or public body in reprisal for a public interest disclosure`
    `something else`

§§ `ss 13 to 17 -- to whom a disclosure may or must be made`

DECLARE `Receiving entity` IS ONE OF
    `the IBAC`
    `the Ombudsman`
    `Integrity Oversight Victoria`
    `the Integrity and Oversight Committee`
    `the Speaker of the Legislative Assembly`
    `the President of the Legislative Council`
    `Victoria Police`
    `the Judicial Commission`
    `the Chief Municipal Inspector`
    `the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission`
    `a public service body`
    `a prescribed public officer`
    `a Council`
    `Gellung Warl`
    `the Chairpersons of the First Peoples' Assembly, or a person named in Gellung Warl's procedures`
    `some other person or body`

DECLARE `Whom it relates to` IS ONE OF
    `Integrity Oversight Victoria or an Integrity Oversight Victoria Officer`
    `the IBAC, an IBAC Officer or a Public Interest Monitor`
    `a judicial officer, or a member of VCAT who is not a judicial officer`
    `a member of Victoria Police personnel other than the Chief Commissioner`
    `the Information Commissioner or the Health Complaints Commissioner`
    `a Councillor`
    `a member of the First Peoples' Assembly`
    `an Examiner, an Ombudsman officer, a VAGO officer, a Judicial Commission officer, or the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission or its people`
    `the Chief Commissioner of Police or another office holder listed in s 14(g)`
    `a member of the Legislative Assembly, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary`
    `a member of the Legislative Council, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary`
    `a Minister who is not a member of Parliament`
    `a public service body or its members, officers or employees`
    `a Council or its officers or employees`
    `Gellung Warl, its staff, or a Nyerna Yoorrook Telkuna or Nginma Ngainga Wara member`
    `the Chief Executive Officer of Gellung Warl`
    `an employee, delegate or agent of a prescribed public officer`
    `any other person or body`

DECLARE `Route facts` HAS
    `the disclosure relates to`                               IS A `Whom it relates to`
    `the entity it is made to`                                IS A `Receiving entity`
    `the discloser belongs to that entity`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the discloser belongs to a Council`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `that entity is the one the conduct relates to`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it concerns a service of a prescribed entity`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 14 ("must be made") and s 17 ("must be made"): the subjects whose disclosures have a required destination.
GIVEN w IS A `Whom it relates to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 14, 17 -- a required subject` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `a public service body or its members, officers or employees` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Council or its officers or employees` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Gellung Warl, its staff, or a Nyerna Yoorrook Telkuna or Nginma Ngainga Wara member` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Chief Executive Officer of Gellung Warl` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an employee, delegate or agent of a prescribed public officer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other person or body` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The destinations s 14 (a) to (g) and s 17 (1) to (3) allow, subject by subject. A "Presiding Officer" (s 14(a)) is the
-- Speaker or the President (s 3).
GIVEN w IS A `Whom it relates to`, e IS A `Receiving entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 14, 17 -- a required destination` w e MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `Integrity Oversight Victoria or an Integrity Oversight Victoria Officer` THEN elem e (LIST `the Integrity and Oversight Committee`, `the Speaker of the Legislative Assembly`, `the President of the Legislative Council`)
    WHEN `the IBAC, an IBAC Officer or a Public Interest Monitor` THEN e EQUALS `Integrity Oversight Victoria`
    WHEN `a judicial officer, or a member of VCAT who is not a judicial officer` THEN elem e (LIST `the IBAC`, `the Judicial Commission`)
    WHEN `a member of Victoria Police personnel other than the Chief Commissioner` THEN elem e (LIST `the IBAC`, `Victoria Police`)
    WHEN `the Information Commissioner or the Health Complaints Commissioner` THEN elem e (LIST `the IBAC`, `the Ombudsman`)
    WHEN `a Councillor` THEN elem e (LIST `the IBAC`, `the Ombudsman`, `the Chief Municipal Inspector`)
    WHEN `a member of the First Peoples' Assembly` THEN elem e (LIST `the IBAC`, `the Ombudsman`)
    WHEN `an Examiner, an Ombudsman officer, a VAGO officer, a Judicial Commission officer, or the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission or its people` THEN elem e (LIST `the IBAC`, `Integrity Oversight Victoria`)
    WHEN `the Chief Commissioner of Police or another office holder listed in s 14(g)` THEN e EQUALS `the IBAC`
    WHEN `a member of the Legislative Assembly, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary` THEN elem e (LIST `the Speaker of the Legislative Assembly`, `the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission`, `the IBAC`)
    WHEN `a member of the Legislative Council, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary` THEN elem e (LIST `the President of the Legislative Council`, `the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission`, `the IBAC`)
    WHEN `a Minister who is not a member of Parliament` THEN elem e (LIST `the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission`, `the IBAC`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN w IS A `Whom it relates to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`relates to a member of Parliament` w MEANS
    elem w (LIST `a member of the Legislative Assembly, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary`, `a member of the Legislative Council, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary`)

-- s 13(2) the IBAC, the Ombudsman, Integrity Oversight Victoria; (3), (4) a public service body about its own conduct, not
-- a prescribed entity's service; (5) a prescribed public officer about their employees, delegates and agents.
GIVEN r IS A `Route facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13 -- a general route` r MEANS
        elem (r's `the entity it is made to`) (LIST `the IBAC`, `the Ombudsman`, `Integrity Oversight Victoria`)
    OR (    r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `a public service body`
        AND r's `the disclosure relates to` EQUALS `a public service body or its members, officers or employees`
        AND r's `that entity is the one the conduct relates to`
        AND (NOT r's `it concerns a service of a prescribed entity`))
    OR (    r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `a prescribed public officer`
        AND r's `the disclosure relates to` EQUALS `an employee, delegate or agent of a prescribed public officer`
        AND r's `that entity is the one the conduct relates to`)

-- s 15: a member, officer or employee may disclose to their own public service body (2) or prescribed public officer
-- (3), "including a disclosure that otherwise is required to be made to another entity under section 14 or 17(3)" (1),
-- but not one that "relates to a member of Parliament" (4).
GIVEN r IS A `Route facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- the insider route` r MEANS
        elem (r's `the entity it is made to`) (LIST `a public service body`, `a prescribed public officer`)
    AND r's `the discloser belongs to that entity`
    AND (NOT `relates to a member of Parliament` (r's `the disclosure relates to`))

-- s 16(1): about a Council, to that Council or the Chief Municipal Inspector; (2): by a member, officer or employee of a
-- Council, to the Council or the Chief Municipal Inspector, "unless" required elsewhere under s 14 or 17(3) or about a
-- member of Parliament (fork F4: a Councillor is not reached through s 16(1)).
GIVEN r IS A `Route facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16 -- Councils` r MEANS
        (    r's `the disclosure relates to` EQUALS `a Council or its officers or employees`
         AND (   r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `the Chief Municipal Inspector`
              OR (r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `a Council` AND r's `that entity is the one the conduct relates to`)))
    OR (    (   (r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `a Council` AND r's `the discloser belongs to that entity`)
             OR (r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `the Chief Municipal Inspector` AND r's `the discloser belongs to a Council`))
        AND (NOT `ss 14, 17 -- a required subject` (r's `the disclosure relates to`)))

-- s 16A(1): about Gellung Warl and its people, to Gellung Warl; (2): about its Chief Executive Officer, to the
-- Chairpersons of the First Peoples' Assembly or a person named in the procedures; (3): by one of its people, to Gellung
-- Warl, "unless" required elsewhere or about a member of Parliament.
GIVEN r IS A `Route facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16A -- Gellung Warl` r MEANS
        (    r's `the disclosure relates to` EQUALS `Gellung Warl, its staff, or a Nyerna Yoorrook Telkuna or Nginma Ngainga Wara member`
         AND r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `Gellung Warl`)
    OR (    r's `the disclosure relates to` EQUALS `the Chief Executive Officer of Gellung Warl`
        AND r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `the Chairpersons of the First Peoples' Assembly, or a person named in Gellung Warl's procedures`)
    OR (    r's `the entity it is made to` EQUALS `Gellung Warl`
        AND r's `the discloser belongs to that entity`
        AND (NOT `ss 14, 17 -- a required subject` (r's `the disclosure relates to`)))

-- Division 2 as a whole: where s 14 or s 17 requires a destination, only that destination or the s 15 insider route;
-- otherwise s 13 and the routes of ss 15, 16, 16A (fork F3 on s 13(1)).
GIVEN r IS A `Route facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Division 2 -- the entity may receive it` r MEANS
    IF `ss 14, 17 -- a required subject` (r's `the disclosure relates to`)
    THEN `ss 14, 17 -- a required destination` (r's `the disclosure relates to`) (r's `the entity it is made to`) OR `s 15 -- the insider route` r
    ELSE `s 13 -- a general route` r OR `s 15 -- the insider route` r OR `s 16 -- Councils` r OR `s 16A -- Gellung Warl` r

-- s 18(1)(a): "the receiving entity is an entity to which a public interest disclosure may be made under this Division".
-- Every entity in the list is one, for some disclosure, except "some other person or body".
GIVEN e IS A `Receiving entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Division 2 entity` e MEANS NOT (e EQUALS `some other person or body`)

§§ `s 12 and Schedule 2 -- who may receive a disclosure for an entity`

DECLARE `Who received it` IS ONE OF
    `the entity itself, at its office`
    `an IBAC Officer, Ombudsman officer or Integrity Oversight Victoria Officer of that entity, the Director of the Judicial Commission, or a member of the Integrity and Oversight Committee`
    `a member of Victoria Police personnel of the rank of sergeant or above, including acting`
    `the Head or Chief Executive Officer of the body`
    `a person named in the body's procedures as one who may receive disclosures`
    `my direct or indirect manager or supervisor`
    `someone else`

GIVEN e IS A `Receiving entity`, p IS A `Who received it`, `the discloser is a member of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 -- a permitted person` e p `the discloser is a member of it` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the entity itself, at its office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an IBAC Officer, Ombudsman officer or Integrity Oversight Victoria Officer of that entity, the Director of the Judicial Commission, or a member of the Integrity and Oversight Committee` THEN elem e (LIST `the IBAC`, `the Ombudsman`, `Integrity Oversight Victoria`, `the Judicial Commission`, `the Integrity and Oversight Committee`)
    WHEN `a member of Victoria Police personnel of the rank of sergeant or above, including acting` THEN e EQUALS `Victoria Police`
    WHEN `the Head or Chief Executive Officer of the body` THEN elem e (LIST `a public service body`, `a Council`, `Gellung Warl`)
    WHEN `a person named in the body's procedures as one who may receive disclosures` THEN elem e (LIST `a public service body`, `a Council`, `Gellung Warl`)
    WHEN `my direct or indirect manager or supervisor` THEN elem e (LIST `Victoria Police`, `a public service body`, `a Council`, `Gellung Warl`) AND `the discloser is a member of it`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 3, 43 -- detrimental action in reprisal`

-- s 3 "detrimental action includes" (a) to (c): an open list, so another kind is NOTHING.
DECLARE `Kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `action causing injury, loss or damage`
    `intimidation or harassment`
    `discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in my employment, career, profession, trade or business, including discipline`
    `some other action`

DECLARE `Reprisal facts` HAS
    `the kind of action taken or threatened`                    IS A `Kind of action`
    `the disclosure is one Part 6 protects`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reason was a disclosure or cooperation with an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person treated so made the disclosure`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person contravened s 72 in making it`                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 43(1): "a person takes detrimental action against another person in reprisal for a public interest disclosure if"
-- (a) they take or threaten it, or (b) incite or permit it, "because, or in the belief that" the other person or anyone
-- else made or intends to make the disclosure, or cooperated or intends to cooperate with an investigation. An "if", so
-- no such reason is JUST FALSE. s 43(2): "does not take detrimental action ... if the other person has contravened
-- section 72(1) or (2)", a flat negative, JUST FALSE. The disclosure is a "public interest disclosure" in the Part 6
-- sense (s 38(2)); where it is not, the Act's reprisal provisions do not reach the case: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own
-- wording* (other law may protect: s 7).
GIVEN r IS A `Reprisal facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43 -- detrimental action in reprisal` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT r's `the disclosure is one Part 6 protects`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 38(2))
           IF r's `the person treated so made the disclosure` AND r's `that person contravened s 72 in making it` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT r's `a reason was a disclosure or cooperation with an investigation`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF r's `the kind of action taken or threatened` EQUALS `some other action` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open list: s 3 "includes")
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 24 -- the receiving entity's duty to advise the discloser`

DECLARE `What became of the duty to advise me` IS ONE OF
    `the Act puts no duty to advise me on these facts`
    `advised in time`
    `not advised in time`
    `the time to advise me is still running`

DECLARE `Receiving party` IS ONE OF
    `the receiving entity`

DECLARE `Receiving party's act` IS ONE OF
    `advise the discloser in writing (s 24)`

-- s 24(2), (3): the receiving entity "must advise the person who made the disclosure"; (4) the advice "must be (a) in
-- writing; and (b) given no later than 28 days after the disclosure is made to the receiving entity".
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Receiving party` `Receiving party's act`
`the receiving entity must advise me in time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the receiving entity`
    MUST `advise the discloser in writing (s 24)`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the receiving entity` BECAUSE "the receiving entity did not advise the person who made the disclosure in writing within 28 days after it was made (s 24(4) of the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012)"

-- The trace helper, in the shape of the Health Complaints Act 2016 encoding's. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an
-- EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the advice was given, FULFILLED means in time and anything else
-- late; where it was not, the helper asks whether advising today would still be in time.
GIVEN `the days allowed`       IS A NUMBER
      `it has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time it was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty to advise me`
`what became of the duty to advise` `the days allowed` `it has been done` `the time it was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the receiving entity must advise me in time` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `the receiving entity` `advise the discloser in writing (s 24)` `the time it was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `advised in time`
         OTHERWISE `not advised in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the receiving entity must advise me in time` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the receiving entity` `advise the discloser in writing (s 24)` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the time to advise me is still running`
         OTHERWISE `not advised in time`

§§ `ss 52 to 54 -- confidentiality`

-- s 3 "assessable disclosure means" (a) to (h).
DECLARE `How it reached the integrity bodies` IS ONE OF
    `made to the IBAC under Division 2 of Part 2`
    `made to Integrity Oversight Victoria under s 14(b)`
    `made to the Integrity and Oversight Committee under s 14(a)`
    `made to another entity that must notify it for assessment under s 21(2)`
    `a police complaint disclosure that must be notified to the IBAC under s 22, or made to the IBAC`
    `a related disclosure that must be notified under s 36(2)`
    `none of these, so not an assessable disclosure`

-- Why the information was passed on: the exceptions of s 52(3), s 53(2) and the circumstances of s 54(2).
DECLARE `Why it was passed on` IS ONE OF
    `with my written consent, by the investigating entity, the Integrity and Oversight Committee or its investigator, as I consented`
    `by direction or authorisation of the investigating entity investigating the disclosure`
    `to the extent necessary for lawful action about the conduct disclosed, including discipline`
    `after a determination that the disclosure is not a public interest complaint`
    `after an investigating entity or the Integrity and Oversight Committee lawfully published it in a report to Parliament`
    `after an investigating entity otherwise lawfully made it public`
    `where necessary to exercise functions under this Act`
    `by an investigating entity or its officer, where necessary to investigate a public interest complaint`
    `to Victoria Police, about criminal conduct an investigating entity already raised with the Chief Commissioner`
    `for a proceeding for an offence against a relevant Act`
    `for a disciplinary process about conduct that could be an offence against a relevant Act`
    `for a restorative engagement process, with the written consent of the person alleging sex discrimination or sexual harassment`
    `to obtain legal advice or representation about a witness summons, a confidentiality notice, or rights and obligations under a relevant Act`
    `by a lawyer so consulted, to meet a legal duty of disclosure or a professional obligation`
    `to an interpreter, so that someone without enough English can comply`
    `to a parent, guardian or independent person, so that someone under 18 can comply`
    `to an independent person, so that someone illiterate or with an impairment can comply`
    `to a registered health practitioner, my trade union or an employee assistance program, to help me get advice or support`
    `to the Victorian WorkCover Authority for a workers' compensation claim`
    `to a prescribed service for its prescribed purpose`
    `for an application to the Fair Work Commission`
    `none of these`

-- s 54(2) (a) to (m).
GIVEN w IS A `Why it was passed on`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54 -- a permitted circumstance` w MEANS
    elem w (LIST
        `where necessary to exercise functions under this Act`,
        `by an investigating entity or its officer, where necessary to investigate a public interest complaint`,
        `to Victoria Police, about criminal conduct an investigating entity already raised with the Chief Commissioner`,
        `for a proceeding for an offence against a relevant Act`,
        `for a disciplinary process about conduct that could be an offence against a relevant Act`,
        `for a restorative engagement process, with the written consent of the person alleging sex discrimination or sexual harassment`,
        `to obtain legal advice or representation about a witness summons, a confidentiality notice, or rights and obligations under a relevant Act`,
        `by a lawyer so consulted, to meet a legal duty of disclosure or a professional obligation`,
        `to an interpreter, so that someone without enough English can comply`,
        `to a parent, guardian or independent person, so that someone under 18 can comply`,
        `to an independent person, so that someone illiterate or with an impairment can comply`,
        `to a registered health practitioner, my trade union or an employee assistance program, to help me get advice or support`,
        `to the Victorian WorkCover Authority for a workers' compensation claim`,
        `to a prescribed service for its prescribed purpose`,
        `for an application to the Fair Work Commission`)

-- s 52(3): (a)(i) s 54, (ii) direction or authorisation, (iii) lawful action; (b) after a "not a public interest
-- complaint" determination; (c) after an investigating entity's report to Parliament or other publication; (d) after
-- the Committee's report to Parliament. No consent exception.
GIVEN w IS A `Why it was passed on`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(3) -- an exception for the content` w MEANS
        `s 54 -- a permitted circumstance` w
    OR elem w (LIST
        `by direction or authorisation of the investigating entity investigating the disclosure`,
        `to the extent necessary for lawful action about the conduct disclosed, including discipline`,
        `after a determination that the disclosure is not a public interest complaint`,
        `after an investigating entity or the Integrity and Oversight Committee lawfully published it in a report to Parliament`,
        `after an investigating entity otherwise lawfully made it public`)

-- s 53(2): (a), (ab) written consent; (b) s 54; (c) after a "not a public interest complaint" determination; (d) after
-- an investigating entity's report to Parliament or other publication; (e) after the Committee's report to Parliament.
-- No exception for a direction or for lawful action (finding 6).
GIVEN w IS A `Why it was passed on`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(2) -- an exception for my identity` w MEANS
        `s 54 -- a permitted circumstance` w
    OR elem w (LIST
        `with my written consent, by the investigating entity, the Integrity and Oversight Committee or its investigator, as I consented`,
        `after a determination that the disclosure is not a public interest complaint`,
        `after an investigating entity or the Integrity and Oversight Committee lawfully published it in a report to Parliament`,
        `after an investigating entity otherwise lawfully made it public`)

§§ `Offences and penalties`

-- The offences a person meets around a disclosure, with the maximum penalty. The value of a penalty unit is fixed under
-- the Monetary Units Act 2004, not deposited: the answer is in penalty units. s 81 (the Whistleblowers Protection Act
-- 2001's transitional offence) is out.
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 45 -- detrimental action in reprisal for a public interest disclosure`
    `s 52 -- disclosing the content of an assessable disclosure`
    `s 53 -- disclosing information likely to identify the person who made an assessable disclosure`
    `s 72(1) -- giving information known to be false or misleading, meant to be acted on as a public interest disclosure`
    `s 72(2) -- giving further information known to be false or misleading`
    `s 73(1) -- falsely claiming a matter is the subject of a public interest disclosure`
    `s 73(2) -- falsely claiming a matter is the subject of a disclosure determined to be a public interest complaint`

-- ss 52, 53: "In the case of a natural person, 120 penalty units ...; In the case of a body corporate, 600 penalty units".
-- s 45: "240 penalty units or 2 years imprisonment or both"; ss 72, 73: "120 penalty units or 12 months imprisonment or
-- both", with no figure for a body corporate. For a body corporate on those the Act is silent (a general rule elsewhere,
-- not deposited, may set one): NOTHING-kind *silent* (finding 9).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum penalty units for` `the offence` `a body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 45 -- detrimental action in reprisal for a public interest disclosure` THEN `units` 240
    WHEN `s 52 -- disclosing the content of an assessable disclosure` THEN `units with a corporate figure` 120 600
    WHEN `s 53 -- disclosing information likely to identify the person who made an assessable disclosure` THEN `units with a corporate figure` 120 600
    OTHERWISE `units` 120
    WHERE
        GIVEN `natural` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
        `units` `natural` MEANS IF `a body corporate` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `natural` -- NOTHING-kind (silent: no body corporate figure)
        GIVEN `natural` IS A NUMBER, `corporate` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
        `units with a corporate figure` `natural` `corporate` MEANS IF `a body corporate` THEN JUST `corporate` ELSE JUST `natural`

-- Imprisonment, natural persons only: s 45 "2 years" (24 months); ss 52, 53 (natural person), 72, 73 "12 months".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for` `the offence` `a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a body corporate`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `s 45 -- detrimental action in reprisal for a public interest disclosure` THEN 24
         OTHERWISE 12
